## CHECKLIST PARA NUEVOS SERVICIOS

Cuando crees un nuevo servicio, asegura:

- [ ] `pytest` y `pytest-asyncio` en requirements.txt
- [ ] Test de `/health` endpoint
- [ ] Test de model loading
- [ ] Test de inference básica
- [ ] Tests de error handling (invalid inputs)
- [ ] Coverage >80% para código nuevo (aspiracional)
- [ ] Fixtures para setup común
- [ ] Integration test end-to-end (opcional)

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS (PROHIBIDOS)

### ❌ NEVER:
- Omitir tests en nuevos servicios
- Tests que requieren conexión a internet (mocking!)
- Tests que modifican archivos de producción
- Hardcodear paths absolutos en tests
- Tests que dependen de orden de ejecución
- Tests sin assertions
- Ignorar test failures ("lo arreglaré después")

---

## EJEMPLOS COMPLETOS

### Ejemplo: test_main.py completo

```python
from fastapi.testclient import TestClient
import pytest
from app.main import app

client = TestClient(app)

class TestHealthEndpoint:
    def test_health_returns_200(self):
        response = client.get("/health")
        assert response.status_code == 200
    
    def test_health_response_structure(self):
        response = client.get("/health")
        data = response.json()
        
        assert "status" in data
        assert "model_loaded" in data
        assert "device" in data
        assert "timestamp" in data

class TestAnalyzeEndpoint:
    def test_analyze_requires_file(self):
        response = client.post("/analyze")
        assert response.status_code == 422  # Unprocessable Entity
    
    def test_analyze_rejects_non_image(self):
        response = client.post(
            "/analyze",
            files={"file": ("test.txt", b"text", "text/plain")}
        )
        assert response.status_code == 400
    
    @pytest.mark.asyncio
    async def test_analyze_with_valid_image(self):
        with open("tests/fixtures/test_image.jpg", "rb") as f:
            response = client.post(
                "/analyze",
                files={"file": ("test.jpg", f, "image/jpeg")}
            )
        
        assert response.status_code == 200
        data = response.json()
        assert "results" in data
```

